This use of two arbitrary points of a line to compute its slope leads to the following most general definition of the slope of a line.

**Definition** Let (x0, yo) and (XI, yj) be arbitrary points on a line e. The ratio

$$m = \frac{y_1 - y_0}{x_1 - x_0}$$

