# **The Plane**

In some of our economic examples. we have used pairs of numbers to represent economic objects, for example, consumption bundles in Chapter 1. Pairs of numbers also have a geometric representation, called the **Cartesian plane or Euclidean Z-space,** and written as **R2.** To depict **R',** first draw two pcrpcndicular number lines: one horizontal to represent the first **component x1** of the pair (x1, x2) and the other vertical to represent the second component x2 of (x,, x2). The unit length is usually the same along each line (although it need not be). These two

