In studying sequences, one often must consider the subsequences of a given sequence. To define the concept of a subsequence carefully. think of a sequence as the image of a function *F* from the nature1 numbers to the real numbcrs, where we write F(n) as x,,. Now, let M be any infinite subset of the natural numbers. Write *M as {n,, n2, ni,. .},* where

$$n_1 < n_2 < n_3 <$$

