at the solution  $x = 1, y = 4, u = 1, v = -1$ . Think of  $u$  and  $v$  as exogenous and  $x$  and  $y$  as endogenous. Use calculus to estimate the values of  $x$  and  $y$  that correspond to  $u = .9$  and  $v = -1.1$ .

