$$2xz + xy + z - 2\sqrt{z} = 11 \quad xyz = 6$$

is satisfied. One solution of this set of equations is  $x = 3, y = 2, z = 1$ , and Northern Saskatchewan is in equilibrium at this point. Suppose that the prime minister discovers that the variable  $z$  (output of beaver pelts) can be controlled by simple decree.

a) If the prime minister raises  $z$  to 1.1, use calculus to estimate the change in  $x$  and  $y$ .  
 b) If  $x$  were in the control of the prime minister and not  $y$  or  $z$ , explain why you cannot use this method to estimate the effect of reducing  $x$  from 3 to 2.95.

