as defining some endogenous variables in terms of some exogenous variables.

a) Divide the three variables into exogenous ones and endogenous ones in a neighborhood of  $x = 2, y = 1, z = 1$  so that the Implicit Function Theorem applies.  
 b) If each of the exogenous variables in your answer to a) increases by 0.25, use calculus to estimate how each of the endogenous variables will change.

