Top Diagram: Shows an upward-opening paraboloid intersected by a horizontal plane labeled {x_3 = 1}. The intersection forms a closed ellipse (or circle), highlighted with a thick dark boundary curve around the surface where it meets the plane.

Bottom Diagram: Shows a saddle-like / hyperbolic surface intersected by a horizontal plane labeled {x_3 = 1}. The intersection forms two hyperbolic curves on opposite sides of the surface, outlined with thick dark lines, demonstrating how the level set produces hyperbolas.

