23.33 Suppose that the weather in Ann Arbor in July can be characterized as sunny, rainy, or cloudy (with no rain). By looking up back issues of the *Ann Arbor News*, we estimate that if it is sunny on a July day, it is equally likely to be sunny or cloudy on the next day, but it won't rain. If a July day is cloudy, there is a 50 percent chance that it will rain on the next day, a 25 percent chance that it will be sunny, and a 25 percent chance that it will remain cloudy without rain. If it rains on a July day, it won't be sunny the next day, and there is a 50-50 chance of continued rain.

1. Write out the corresponding Markov system.
2. Show that the underlying matrix is regular.
