**26.21** (difficult) Suppose that you are given a square matrix  $A$ , partitioned into four submatrices:

$$A = \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & A_{12} \\ A_{21} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix}$$

where  $A_{11}$  and  $A_{22}$  are square submatrices.

a) Show that

$$\det \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & \mathbf{0} \\ \mathbf{0} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} = \det A_{11} \cdot \det A_{22}.$$

b) Show that

$$\det \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & A_{12} \\ \mathbf{0} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} = \det \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & \mathbf{0} \\ A_{21} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} = \det A_{11} \cdot \det A_{22}.$$

