$$\begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & A_{12} \\ A_{21} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} - A_{12}A_{22}^{-1}A_{21} & A_{12} \\ \mathbf{0} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} I & \mathbf{0} \\ A_{22}^{-1}A_{21} & I \end{pmatrix}.$$

d) Conclude that if  $A_{22}$  is nonsingular,

$$\det \begin{pmatrix} A_{11} & A_{12} \\ A_{21} & A_{22} \end{pmatrix} = \det(A_{11} - A_{12}A_{22}^{-1}A_{21}) \cdot \det A_{22}.$$

e) Use this method to compute

$$\det \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\ 1 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\ -3 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\ 4 & 2 & 5 & 2 \end{pmatrix}.$$

