**A5.2** What is the expected value and variance for the toss of a single die? If you win \$2 times the face value of your toss, what is your expected winning?

**A5.3** What is the expected value and variance of the toss of two dies? If you win an amount equal to the absolute value of the difference in the face values of the die, what is your expected winning?

**A5.4** Suppose that you take \$1000 along for spending money on a trip to New York City. Your utility from the trip is given by the function  $U(y) = y^{1/3}$  of the amount  $y$  you spend. Suppose that there is a 10 percent chance that you will lose \$100 during the trip and a 90 percent chance that you will be able to spend all \$1000.

1. What is the expected utility of your trip?

<!-- page 866 -->

- b) What is your expected utility if you buy \$100 worth of traveler's checks, as certain insurance against the loss, for an actuarily fair premium of \$10?
- c) What is the most you would pay from an expected utility point of view for insurance against that loss of \$100?

**A5.5** Use the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to derive the formulas (5) and (6) for the mean and variance of a continuous random variable.

